WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.943
In tutorial 1.5, you'll choose the
search you most want to be found for,

00:00:10.993 --> 00:00:13.079
so your pages are the ones you want.

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:17.444
First, type a search a
customer would use to find you.

00:00:17.494 --> 00:00:20.629
Click Check it to see how hard
that search is for your site.

00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:26.698
Your result shows your chances, how
many people search for it each month,

00:00:26.748 --> 00:00:28.788
and about how many pages it takes.

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:35.409
If your search names a place outside
your main country, Alaventra asks first.

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:40.140
Take the suggested search, keep yours,
or click Cancel and type another.

00:00:41.151 --> 00:00:46.626
Or start from our suggestions. Each card
shows how many people search, your chances,

00:00:46.676 --> 00:00:48.508
and the credits a page uses.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.176
Click Choose this keyword
on the one you want.

00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:54.540
Our first pick is the one we'd start with.

00:00:56.605 --> 00:01:00.080
Then choose how pages are
written: a new page each week,

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.478
or each page only after your OK.

00:01:04.676 --> 00:01:08.606
Next, pick how much we do on our
own. Two days before each week,

00:01:08.656 --> 00:01:11.294
you see what's coming up,
and you can skip anything.

00:01:13.651 --> 00:01:17.241
Finally, click Continue with
this choice. Not sure yet?

00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:20.084
Click I'll choose later,
and pick from the Pipeline.

00:01:21.155 --> 00:01:23.805
Nothing is written until
you finish the setup.

00:01:23.855 --> 00:01:26.210
Next, you choose what to check each week.

00:01:28.126 --> 00:01:32.926
So, type a search and check it, or pick a
suggestion, choose how pages are written,

00:01:32.976 --> 00:01:35.262
pick how much we do, and continue.

00:01:36.245 --> 00:01:42.432
Your first keyword is chosen. Next, choose
what to track and start, in tutorial 1.6.
